editorialMd:
The working idea

links is a square directed adjacency matrix: 0 means no edge, and a positive value is its cost. From vertex 0, produce each vertex's minimum total cost in vertex order, using -1 for unreachable vertices. The empty graph produces no costs.

Return only the strictly positive values in the derived sequence, preserving their relative order and duplicates.

Why this works

Each derived value follows the unit's stated order and includes exactly the items allowed by its definition. The receipt then folds or filters those values without changing their meaning. Check the empty, singleton, repeated and maximum-size inputs before trusting the final total.

Target time O(V^2 + E log V); space O(n).

javascript
function weightedLinesPositiveProofStrip(links, k) {
  const a=links; let out=[];
  const n=a.length,dist=Array(n).fill(Infinity),heap=[];if(n){dist[0]=0;heap.push([0,0]);}while(heap.length){const [cost,u]=heap[0],last=heap.pop();if(heap.length){heap[0]=last;let i=0;while(true){let j=i,l=i*2+1,r=l+1;if(l<heap.length&&heap[l][0]<heap[j][0])j=l;if(r<heap.length&&heap[r][0]<heap[j][0])j=r;if(j===i)break;[heap[i],heap[j]]=[heap[j],heap[i]];i=j;}}if(cost!==dist[u])continue;for(let v=0;v<n;v++)if(a[u][v]>0&&cost+a[u][v]<dist[v]){dist[v]=cost+a[u][v];heap.push([dist[v],v]);let i=heap.length-1;while(i>0){const p=(i-1)>>1;if(heap[p][0]<=heap[i][0])break;[heap[p],heap[i]]=[heap[i],heap[p]];i=p;}}}out=dist.map(x=>Number.isFinite(x)?x:-1);
  return out.filter(x=>x>0);
}


